\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue}\uwave {FedRAS system architecture and round pipeline. The edge aggregator estimates client link states, scores every client--rank pair with the delivery hazard \eqref  {eq:hazard} and the saturating capacity \eqref  {eq:cap}, and computes the client--rank assignment with the exact grid-based dynamic program under the byte budget and the admission cap (Proposition~\ref {prop:dp}). Admitted clients train on a frozen backbone with LoRA factors sliced to the assigned rank and upload only the trainable factor $B$, at 5.63\,KB per rank column; the shared factor $A$ is never transmitted. Updates arriving within the deadline $\tau $ pass the on-time gate and are aggregated rank-maskedly while $A$ stays frozen (Proposition~\ref {prop:agg}); late or lost updates are discarded, and the observed outcomes update the link-state history.}}}}{6}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{6}{}{}{}}
